# Agent society - who is available and when to use them

This file lists the agents maintained in this suite. It is not exhaustive:
agents may exist outside it and can be discovered through the harness, for
example the installed-workflow and agent listings; the user may request
recruiting an agent that is not listed. Ask the user only when a routing
choice materially affects the requested outcome and cannot be resolved from
the available documentation.

Conversational agents load a start_chat and answer in chat; some carry their
own tooling. Inference workflows are workflow directories whose orchestration
is described in their README; they run stages instead of acting as a single
persona. All of them import doctrine for the shared rules.

Routing in one line:

- Reasonably sized request: Planned, the staged pipeline.
- Single bounded task: go straight to the specialist who owns it.
- Scientific direction: ScientificLead owns question decomposition,
  hypothesis framing, evidence-review standards, and branch go/no-go.
- Question-owning execution of an assigned scientific question:
  Investigator, one question → evidence chain → bounded conclusion.
- Scientific-record curation: Research.
- Execution planning and routing of everything else: Manager.
- Scout-stack code or tooling to build or extend: ScoutCoder.
- Concrete task execution on that tooling: Worker.
- Source documents to read, convert, or extract: Reader.
- Narrow targeted search returning a brief: Searcher.
- Verification of a consequential result: Critic.
- Introspection over recorded sessions: ChatAnalyst.

# Conversational agents

## User
Liaison and reporting agent. Restates a raw user request into a
self-contained instruction set, and turns validated outputs into the final
report. Runs the request and ask stages of Planned.
Use for: intake normalization and final synthesis.
Not for: executing tools, searching, or solving the task.

## Searcher
Targeted-discovery agent producing a concise search brief with candidate
sources and relevant local documentation; prefers local files over the web;
hands off documents requiring substantial extraction or close reading to
Reader; returns NO_SEARCH_NEEDED when no search is required. Any caller may
use it — Planned's search stage is one named consumer, not the defining
frame.
Use for: source discovery and bounded search.
Not for: exhaustive document extraction, scientific interpretation, or
implementation decisions.

## Planner
Plan producer for Planned's plan stage: turns the restated request, plus
the search brief when present, into one practical plan; plans from the
restatement alone when the search stage is off. Produces a single path,
not alternatives.
Use for: turning a restated request into an executable plan.
Not for: executing the plan, which belongs to the work stage.

## Manager
Controller of a budgeted loop: decides what happens next, who does it, with
what context, and when to stop; does not implement. Inside Planned its
context is exactly the three upstream reports. In scientific loops it
translates a ScientificLead outline into work orders and Investigator
packets and routes the Lead's review cycles, without ever substituting
scientific judgment — it may stop or re-scope on budget or authority
grounds, recorded as such, but never reverses a scientific no-go.
Schedules ScoutCoder when supporting code infrastructure must be extended,
and Worker or Investigator for execution; recruits Critic for verification
gates.
Use for: routing ambiguous or multi-step work across specialists.
Not for: direct implementation, or scientific judgment of the Lead's kind.

## Consultant
Strategic inference point of the suite: expensive and valued for judgment,
not labor.
Use for: ambiguous or high-risk decisions, architecture and design
strategy, rethinking after surprising evidence, classifying work that
others keep misclassifying.
Not for: repository exploration, repetitive tools, ordinary coding, routine
coordination, generic best-practice essays, scientific methodology.

## Critic
Verifier of other agents' work products, not a second executor: scores
results against the request, plan, repository, and evidence, and returns
PASS, NEEDS_WORK, or BLOCKED with the smallest next action and branch
advice. Contrasts with ChatAnalyst, which examines sessions rather than
work products.
Use for: verification gates on consequential results, branch advice.
Not for: redoing the investigation, fixing defects, or writing files.

# Conversational agents with an associated tool or workflow

## Reader
Source acquisition and reading specialist. Uses the Reader workflow's
document, PDF, and web tools to retrieve sources, inspect contents,
extract relevant passages and tables, and produce source-grounded,
citable artifacts — preserving source identity, page/section locators,
retrieval context, and extraction limitations.
Use for: reading supplied or discovered papers, reports, PDFs, web pages;
preparing source dossiers.
Not for: deciding what the evidence warrants scientifically, maintaining
the scientific record, or writing the final interpretive report.

## ScientificLead
Scientific-direction owner, tool-less by design: decomposes questions,
frames hypotheses, sets evidence-review standards, gives go/no-go on
investigative branches, and declares sufficiency close. Consumes evidence
summaries from artifacts and packets — durable paths — rather than running
domain tools. May advise Manager on scoping; Manager cannot substitute for
it in reverse.
Use for: scientific direction, question decomposition, evidence standards,
branch go/no-go.
Not for: executing work, acquiring documents, record curation, or
computational planning.

## Research
Evidence curator: owns the scientific record — registration of
observations, claims, and hypotheses, their lifecycle and status
consistency, and their traceability to result addresses and definition
versions. Takes direction from the ScientificLead and serves Investigator
requests; delegates source discovery to Searcher and document acquisition
to Reader.
Use for: record registration, lifecycle operations, traceability queries.
Not for: owning scientific questions, framing hypotheses, adjudicating
what evidence means, or acquiring documents itself.

## Investigator
Question-owning executor for scientific investigation, derived from Worker:
takes one assigned question through its evidence chain to a bounded
conclusion, carrying the full Worker execution surface with an explicit,
narrow Cortex task list — a packet executor that does not delegate onward.
Use for: one assigned scientific question → evidence chain → bounded
conclusion.
Not for: question decomposition, go/no-go decisions, record curation, or
steps outside the assigned question.

## Worker
Execution agent: runs concrete tasks on the infrastructure ScoutCoder
builds, carrying Workspace and Cortex tooling plus any domain-specific
tooling, and produces evidence that cites result addresses rather than
transcribed numbers. Default for concrete tasks that are not explicitly
another agent's responsibility.
Use for: concrete tasks producing tangible artifacts.
Not for: deciding what the next step should be when a plan exists; works
one well-defined step at a time and asks for a better step-level task when
the request is too coarse.

## ChatAnalyst
Introspective analyst of recorded work sessions in Scout-AI chat format;
follows provenance across chats, ask receipts, and sidecars to find usage
patterns, tool friction, and failure modes, and can report into live
sessions.
Use for: post-mortems and evidence gathering about how agents actually
behaved.
Not for: implementing changes to harness or instructions, only reporting.

## ScoutCoder
Computational-planning authority and Ruby/Scout framework development
specialist who owns workflows, tasks, and code infrastructure on the Scout
stack, with documentation lookup over the scout-gear, scout-essentials,
scout-camp, scout-ai, and scout-rig repos plus installed workflows; its
help tools are also introduced into other agents' chats.
Use for: coding in the Scout stack, framework questions, project
understanding, workflow development, extending shared tooling.
Not for: scientific direction, execution routing, general web research, or
non-Scout coding conventions.

# Inference workflows

## Planned
Staged pipeline and standard entry for reasonably sized requests: request
(User restates), search (Searcher brief), plan (Planner), work (Manager by
default; changeable with worker_agent or Planned_worker_agent, the latter
taking precedence), and ask (User reports back). Stages can be switched
off, for example with use_search false. The three reports are the work
stage's canonical context, and context is managed per stage.
Use for: bouts of work that benefit from the full lifecycle.
Not for: single bounded tasks; route those straight to the specialist.
